    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1299">

                <pb facs="0885" n="769" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg769"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/10612.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Vice Consul Stadden to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Manzanillo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-01-19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 19, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Governor of the State of Colima called a meeting of residents of Colima on
                    the seventeenth instant demanding that 100,000 pesos be furnished at once saying
                    if not furnished voluntarily he would collect by some means. Demonstration
                    caused by the demand, opposition and uprising probable. Representatives of
                    American companies and interests request information as to whether they shall
                    contribute or refuse to contribute. Embassy advised.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stadden</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
